---
description: Rules for the Gemini integration (research + writing of briefings)
globs: scheduler/generator.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use only the official `google-genai` SDK: `genai.Client(api_key=...)` + `client.models.generate_content(...)`.
  `jobs.py` passes the key from `db.get_secret("gemini_api_key")`.
- Never guess SDK class/field names or model IDs. Inspect the installed SDK or check ai.google.dev first.
- Tools: `google_search` + `url_context`. Depth: `thinking_config.thinking_level` from `THINKING_LEVELS[effort]`.
  Keep `THINKING_LEVELS` keys equal to `db.EFFORTS`.
- Never include `part.thought` text. The SDK auto-resumes `CONTINUATION`, so don't add a manual loop.
- `SYSTEM_PROMPT` defines `<summary_json>` (`title, highlights, mood, headlines`), which `jobs.py` and `notify.py`
  use. Change them together.
- Every failure becomes a `GenerationError` with a beginner-friendly fix (429 → turn on billing).
- After changes run `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_generator.py tests/test_jobs.py`.
  No real API calls without asking the user.
